Finally! Ive finally done it! In fact its the first time Ive ever
managed to get all the invocation artifacts, let alone ascend, but
once I maxed out all my armour, prepared myself for it properly (had a
heap of holy water and blessed potions of full healing, in fact way
too much (around 30 of each), so had to drink a heap of full healings
and throw away a heap of holy water), and got the book from Yendor,
the rest of the game was very simple. But anyway, I'll start fro mthe
start, as best I can.
I started this game, as I had started most of my other ones, playing a
'naked, petless tourist' (ie Id ditch my pet ASAP, and dump all of my
equipment either in a container or under a boulder (dont want a
monster getting hold of all my goodies)... prob more that half of the
games I start this way die before lv 3, but if they make it that far,
then its like playing a normal game I find. Anywho, was fairly
cautious, using coridors, making sure I had escape routes, etc... and
had to use them a fair bit untill I got exp lv 3-4... found a dwarvern
short sword, and considering the only other weapons I had were crude
daggers, decided to use that as my main weapon, and eventually got
that skill up to skilled (prob more than I should have, as I was
always going to change weapons once I got an artifact, but oh well),
did the mines, found a couple of dogs, and fed them with some tripe Id
found, and they eventually made it to large dogs... alter in minewtown
was not co-aligned, so just tested my equipment and kept on going
down... grabbed the luckstone, blessed it... stopped at minetown
again, to see if my pets would attack the shopkeepers... as it turned
out they would, so I ordered them to kill them and the guards... they
did that well enough, lost one of the dogs, but oh well... found 2
different lamps in the lighting store, so Id'd them and discovered the
magic lamp... but just used it as a perminant light source, had
alright armour (just mithril, hard hat, hard shoes, etc), grabbed all
the money from the stores (and a magic marker, the 1st of 3 Id find
for the game), bought protection, then killed the priest and got my
money back... converted the alter and got a few useless artifacts, but
eventually got Mojo, which served me well for the rest of the game.
Cleared out the did sokoban and got another amulet of reflection (was
really hoping for boH, I have a habit of carrying more than I need...
in fact I was burdended for all of the game except just before I made
the dash for the amulet, where I polypiled and dumped what I didnt
need)... did my quest and got the PYEC... which is very handy with my
wands... made the mazes in hell a lot easier, they were full of holes
thanks to my ever rechargable wands of digging, found my first temple
in the dungeons around lv 21 (a co-aligned temple), then another
temple at lv 23, so I bought more protection, but couldnt get my naked
AC much below 0 (think I got it to -1 before I resorted to eating some
rings), but I spent around 150k on each one (of course getting my
money back afterwards... by ths stage I had a pretty good AC and wasnt
afraid of hurting my luck my killing a few friendlies... I think I
also managed to get a pet dragon with a saddle and a pet vamp lord
with an AC of -15 thanks to my discarded armour (but they didnt
survive the many poly traps, especially in hell)... the castle was a
piece of cake, didnt even have to use a ring of conflict. Killed the
dragons, but still didnt have any silver scales, so used a wish on
that, one for my speed boots, one for cloak magic resistance (had it
through the PYEC, but I know how the wiz likes to steal it (though he
never did))... and that was it I think, got my AC down to -53 or so,
had mojo and a silver saber I found both to +7 and twoweaponed...
polypiled with some of the stuff I had gathered... then polymorphed
into a rock mole, ate some more rings of protection, rings of damage,
and amulets of magic breathing... took a few goes but finally got all
of thoses (though the ring I really ranted to eat, regeneration, wasnt
edible, even though I had around 6 of them), went down to hell, got
the candle thing from vlad, marked the vibrating square, cleared all
the monsters from yendors tower (but didnt disturb him yet, went back
to the dungeons, tried sacrificing for another artifact (why not?),
though despite the fact I went through 2 wands of create monster
untill I could re-charge them no more, I didnt get anything else (7
had been created in the game so far... but then I later found 3 more
randomly generated in hell, and one more in the astral planes, for 11
all up for the game... though I only used 2), polypiled one more time,
ID'd everything, got a heap of holy water and blessed full healing...
but then had to throw most of it away so I was unburdened. (wanted to
make sure I didnt stuff anything up this late in the game... for all
of the late game I always had 2 AoLS in main inventory (one worn) and
a couple more in my BoH, so with around 20 things of holy water and
the same of blessed full healing, and a handfull of wands of death,
teleport, and digging, I got ready for my race down.
Killed the wizard... tryed zapping him with a WoD twice, but kept on
missing him, so did it the old fashioned way, grabed the book, raced
down for the amulet... but this stage all my pets had either died or
polyed to something stupid, grabbed it, raced up... though in hell I
dropped levels when climbing around 15 times (indluding once which put
me in the middle of a giant pool of water in Jublix's swamp, luck I
had magic breating), but once I got out of hell it never happened
again. Oh, my 12 cursed potion of gain level also helped there... had
virtualy nothing try and stop me, the wiz a few times, but a couple of
hits and he went down... he never even stole anything from me! Went to
the planes, killed the wiz again, got out my c?oGD, found the portal,
dug my way there, killing whatever got in my way with no hassles, fire
was also no problem, though the c?oGD didnt help me, as it showed all
traps as '$', so had to uncurse one, confuse myself, and read it
again... with ring of levitation was no problem, air the same, the air
elements I heard so much about were no problem, had my wands of
teleport and polymorph handy, but never had to use them... and even
chased a few down for fun... water the same thing... however I had no
idea what to expect from the astral plane, so I wished up (oh, Id
eneded up finsing 3 magic lamps, one minetown, one orcus town, and the
other one who knows, and had most of my wishes on my wand still) a
blessed figurine of an archon, same again of a ki-rin, and a blessed
saddle. Used both the figurines, got on my ki-rin, and went to the
astral plane. Went right first, killed death, wrong alter... however
whilst I was surounded by monsters which had been summoned, I confused
myself and read a ?oTM, so instantly had a heap of pets (most
useless), ran to the next alter, again wrong one, ran back, made it to
the last one, called in my pets, and was going to sacrifice, but then
I realised I was near full health, and nothing had been able to damage
me (-53AC will do that), so I decided to go on a killing spree, and
killed everything in sight (the horseman a few times), even friendlies
(my god didnt like my killing his high priest or his angles, but oh
well, he couldnt touch me with my refletion, so chased down every last
creature, then went about collecting their money, found a heap of fake
amulets, and also a +8 Vorpal blade (pitty it was after I killed
everything), then decided to have a bit of fun by sacrificing the hake
amulets... my god didnt like that, sent me a few elements to kill, but
I then decided Id had enough, called my pets around me, and sacrificed
the real thing (oh, not before wishing a few dilithium crystals).
Really, once I made it to the castle and finished off my AK and
enchanted it all, the game was over, the rest was a piece of cake, the
wiz of yendor onl showed upa few times, and his curses likewise, the
elements were a joke, and the astral plane... a little trickier, but
never got below 200HP (max 575), and took just over 11,000 turns
(played it ver safe).
Now for my dump... any sugestions on it more than welcome

Mark, neutral male human Tourist


